  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is because the extent or degree of dissociation increases with increase in dilution of a solution. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mo> </mo><mi>M</mi><mo> </mo><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></math> solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo></math> is most diluted as compared to the other two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></math> solutions. The vant Hoff factor (i) depends on extent of dilution.This confirms answer at (i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8d479075-3b31-47c9-bc2f-e257584d26a5.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 96px;\"/></p>",
